{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the exact-path succession repair at c0df0efd51946c8159f0af7b4057e8f59d832d60 (request/specific-path-succession-current, one commit on reviewed d1dd3d01, two on main c3169d83; exactly the eight cited paths, +216/-49; Rests-On repair request 7ba66209; artifacts rest on promise d47618a1, the request, their d1dd3d01 predecessors and, for the docs, the code artifacts; nothing stale). Review against request 15266; not merged.\n\nAll five blockers from my ratified verdict c5a7de95 are fixed, each pinned by a mutation on a detached checkout. B1: TestMergeFreshPreflightRefusesACrossAuthorPointerAboveARemovedSource (main_test.go:2025) drives mergeCommand into the refusal through a deletion under a stranger's directory pointer and asserts HEAD, workroom head and depth, and reservation absence (:2046-2055); deleting the guard call at main.go:651 now fails it (\"fresh deletion merge error = nil, want reviewed-path refusal\"), where at d1dd3d01 the same mutation was green. B2: the success case is renamed TestMergeFreshPreflightAllowsAWiderPointerAtALandedDestination (:1998) with a comment that matches its body, and the refusal case exists separately. B3: the new account closure (succession.go:161-165) seals a wider covering candidate into leftLive without retiring it and landed routes non-exact paths to it (:176-186); dropping it fails succession_test.go:109 and main_test.go:1013, and the fold no longer emits \"not classified by receipt\" for those entries. B4: rename keeps source-removal semantics and AGENTS.md:75-77, SKILL.md:229-232 and 272-275, architecture.md:831-835 and merge.md:256 now say so; a rename inside a covered directory publishes the directory and destination and retires the directory, as the text states. B5: TestMergeDeleteRepublishesTheWidestCoveringDirectory (succession_test.go:212) goes red when the widest-covering block in removed is deleted. Every earlier red proof survives at its new lines, two new guards are proved, publish.md:19-23 is fixed, and the dead widest fallback and its stale comment are gone. Gates: gofmt, go build, go vet, git diff --check d1dd3d01..c0df0efd clean; go test ./cmd/gs (397 s), ./internal/docset, ./internal/workroom and ./internal/app -count=1 ok; the fold is untouched.\n\nTwo new defects the repair introduced block approval.\n\n1. A healthy in-target wider pointer is now sealed as abandoned, and the fold renders that as a retirement obligation. artifactRetiresForChanges (succession.go:289-303) returns false for a wider pointer over a modified path, so successionPredecessors (:259-268) no longer classifies it as a predecessor even when its commit is in the target world, and it falls through to sibling or abandoned, the two classes merge.md:252-253 reserves for a non-target candidate. Probe against buildNestedCrossAuthorApproval, whose docs artifact stands at the target's own HEAD: the receipt's left_live carries that artifact as class abandoned, the fold marks it verified, and internal/workroom/render.go:141-143 and :180 print \"carries left live at merge: abandoned artifact #8, retirement owed by @reviewer\" for a live, current, in-target directory pointer, the very act this change exists to prevent. The head's own test enshrines it: main_test.go:1022-1024 wants \"abandoned extra tree\" for the artifact standing at the reviewed candidate head. Three unchanged texts are now false: succession.go:98-99 (leftLive is for artifacts \"not in the target world\"), :251-253 (a shipped artifact is a predecessor when its commit is in the target's world), and merge.md:252-253 (both classes scoped to a non-target candidate) beside the new :250. Nothing is retired and no receipt debt forms, but the immutable receipt states a false obligation on every merge. The repair request's item 3 asked for exactly \"sibling or abandoned\", so this is a design call for the requester: either a third class that carries no cleanup obligation for an in-target wider pointer, or scope abandoned to non-target candidates and give in-target wider pointers their own accounting; then fix the three texts.\n\n2. The central new rule has no red proof on the path this repository exercises. Removing the gate from the ancestor arm (succession.go:266, dropping artifactRetiresForChanges from the condition) leaves the whole ./cmd/gs suite green; the only red proof reaches the candidate arm through the extra fixture. Five live artifacts at cmd/gs, one at current main, cover three of this head's own files, so the ancestor arm is the one that fires here. Add a test with an in-target main-ancestor wider directory pointer over a modified file and assert it is not a predecessor.\n\nRecorded, not blocking, carried from the first round and unassigned by 7ba66209: directory-path artifacts are unretireable by a modify-only merge and the repair's answer to that is now the wrong classification above; the log grows one artifact per changed file (181 publishes for a 181-file merge, main_test.go:1012) and no page states the consequence; a comma anywhere in a changed path makes a merge unmergeable (preflightSuccession, and the kernel refuses it too), undocumented and untracked today.\n\nArchitecture: layer seven (cmd/gs merge adapter) only; layer five is untouched and its tests pass. The contract paragraph at architecture.md:829-835 is published in this head and correctly separates landed destinations from removed sources, but merge.md:252-253 and the plan comment at succession.go:98-99 still state the old scope of sibling and abandoned, so the contract change is not carried through.\n\nSecurity: item B1 is now the strongest guard in the file, proved end to end with HEAD, depth and reservation asserted unchanged. Authority is unchanged and unwidened: refuseUnreachableCrossAuthorRetirements reads only plan.retire and leftLive grants nothing, so item 1 has no authority consequence. Path handling stays byte-exact; artifactRetiresForChanges reuses artifactCoversPath. The residual risk is item 1 misleading an actor into hand-retiring a live lineage.\n\nSimplification: assign's widerPath tie-break (succession.go:172) is still dead; removed still scans covering(path, true) and discards the wider matches, then calls covering(path, false) for exactly those; account (:161-165) duplicates assign's first branch (:167-170) verbatim and assign could call it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6f383bf4b476b50e03dbdb193ae93bfde88f67e6","head":"c0df0efd51946c8159f0af7b4057e8f59d832d60","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:de389176ee098cc7f1416605af6bd6b4b445ae80\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e0e9887c6d4c479855fba3280fb2d3c0ca0af05f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}